WEBVTT

00:04.662 --> 00:07.737
This case study comes from an MSHA report titled

00:07.737 --> 00:10.463
Fatal Slip or Fall of Person Accident,

00:10.463 --> 00:14.362
dated June 8, 2023. It happened at a surface crushed

00:14.362 --> 00:18.113
stone plant in Massachusetts. The miner was experienced,

00:18.113 --> 00:20.225
with nearly thirty years in mining,

00:20.225 --> 00:22.325
and he ran that plant every day.

00:23.436 --> 00:26.274
MSHA classified it as a fall. But the reason he

00:26.274 --> 00:28.774
fell was that a machine he was standing on started

00:28.774 --> 00:31.936
up. This is a lockout and blocking accident,

00:31.936 --> 00:34.036
and it's the kind that happens at plants just like

00:34.036 --> 00:34.898
ours.

00:36.030 --> 00:38.955
At this plant, a small magnet belt hung over one

00:38.955 --> 00:41.580
of the main conveyors to pull out scrap metal.

00:41.580 --> 00:43.880
It was about sixteen feet off the ground.

00:43.880 --> 00:46.843
It was run by a timer. Every ten minutes it started

00:46.843 --> 00:49.517
up on its own, without any warning,

00:49.517 --> 00:51.593
to drop the metal it had collected.

00:52.704 --> 00:55.229
Late in the shift, he shut down part of the plant

00:55.229 --> 00:57.541
to do maintenance on that magnet belt.

00:57.541 --> 01:00.854
He climbed up a catwalk, onto one stopped conveyor,

01:00.854 --> 01:03.342
then onto another, and then on top of the magnet

01:03.342 --> 01:06.116
belt itself. The magnet belt had not been shut

01:06.116 --> 01:09.341
off and locked out. Its timer cycled it on,

01:09.341 --> 01:12.079
and he fell about sixteen feet to the ground.

01:12.079 --> 01:13.416
He died the next day.

01:16.750 --> 01:19.450
The first root cause in MSHA's report:

01:19.450 --> 01:22.225
the magnet belt was not de-energized and blocked

01:22.225 --> 01:25.313
against hazardous motion before maintenance started.

01:25.313 --> 01:27.400
The disconnect for that conveyor was not locked

01:27.400 --> 01:30.325
out. Stopping the other belts didn't make the magnet

01:30.325 --> 01:33.225
belt safe. It was still connected to power and

01:33.225 --> 01:35.038
still controlled by the timer.

01:36.184 --> 01:39.284
The federal standard is direct. Repairs or maintenance

01:39.284 --> 01:42.059
are done with the power off and the machinery blocked

01:42.059 --> 01:44.884
against hazardous motion. The only exception is

01:44.884 --> 01:47.384
when the machine has to be running for testing

01:47.384 --> 01:50.347
or adjustment, and then only with effective protection

01:50.347 --> 01:51.834
for the person doing it.

01:52.978 --> 01:55.478
The second root cause was access. There was no

01:55.478 --> 01:58.516
safe way to reach the magnet belt for maintenance.

01:58.516 --> 02:01.216
No platform, no ladder set up for it,

02:01.216 --> 02:03.366
and no written procedure for the job.

02:03.366 --> 02:05.216
So the way to get there was to climb across the

02:05.216 --> 02:08.378
conveyors. After the accident, the mine built work

02:08.378 --> 02:11.641
platforms, provided ladders, wrote a safe-access

02:11.641 --> 02:15.241
procedure, and retrained its miners on de-energizing,

02:15.241 --> 02:17.566
locking out, and blocking equipment.

02:18.688 --> 02:20.650
Notice something about this accident.

02:20.650 --> 02:23.363
It wasn't a big rebuild. It was a small maintenance

02:23.363 --> 02:25.963
job on a machine the miner knew well.

02:25.963 --> 02:28.400
Small jobs are where shortcuts creep in.

02:28.400 --> 02:30.663
It's only a minute. I'll be careful.

02:30.663 --> 02:33.175
The other belts are off. A shortcut can work a

02:33.175 --> 02:36.213
hundred times, and that makes it feel safe,

02:36.213 --> 02:38.888
right up until the timer, or the other person,

02:38.888 --> 02:40.800
or the stored energy catches you.

02:41.927 --> 02:44.139
That's why the rule doesn't change with the size

02:44.139 --> 02:46.276
of the job. If you're going to put any part of

02:46.276 --> 02:48.489
your body where the machine could move,

02:48.489 --> 02:51.601
it gets locked, tagged, and blocked first.

02:54.932 --> 02:57.357
A stopped machine is not a safe machine.

02:57.357 --> 03:00.619
It can start because of a timer, a remote control,

03:00.619 --> 03:03.344
or an automatic start. It can start because someone

03:03.344 --> 03:05.357
else, who doesn't know you're there,

03:05.357 --> 03:07.757
hits the start button. And it can move with no

03:07.757 --> 03:11.019
power at all, from gravity, belt tension,

03:11.019 --> 03:13.544
a load of rock on the belt, or pressure stored

03:13.544 --> 03:15.744
in hydraulic or air lines.

03:16.862 --> 03:19.674
Lockout takes away the power. Blocking takes away

03:19.674 --> 03:22.299
the motion that's left. You need both.

03:23.432 --> 03:26.007
Our own records have the same warning signs.

03:26.007 --> 03:29.657
At Boonesboro in 2018, a worker had his hand on

03:29.657 --> 03:32.257
a tail pulley to reach the set screws while another

03:32.257 --> 03:35.019
employee turned the same pulley. Guarding on moving

03:35.019 --> 03:37.757
parts was cited five times at Boonesboro.

03:37.757 --> 03:40.695
At Clover Bottom, drivers were hurt clearing plugged

03:40.695 --> 03:44.419
bins with a pipe and a bar, and in 2018 a worker

03:44.419 --> 03:47.544
climbed over a conveyor to clean a stopped plant.

03:47.544 --> 03:50.019
Every one of these is a stop, lock out,

03:50.019 --> 03:51.157
and block job.

03:52.274 --> 03:55.049
Take a bridged primary crusher. Allen's approved

03:55.049 --> 03:57.949
method is the hydraulic rock breaker first.

03:57.949 --> 04:00.237
If that doesn't clear it, the crusher is locked

04:00.237 --> 04:03.287
out and blocked before anyone uses an excavator

04:03.287 --> 04:06.436
or other method. Nobody climbs into a crusher,

04:06.436 --> 04:09.949
or onto a feeder or chute, that's only been stopped.

04:09.949 --> 04:11.399
Stopped is not locked.

04:12.524 --> 04:14.262
Now look at it from the other side.

04:14.262 --> 04:16.637
Someday you may be the person who starts a crusher

04:16.637 --> 04:19.062
or a belt. Before starting a crusher,

04:19.062 --> 04:21.249
the operator has to sound a warning that can be

04:21.249 --> 04:24.012
heard over the noise, or use another effective

04:24.012 --> 04:26.499
way to warn everyone who could be hurt.

04:27.627 --> 04:29.939
But a horn only works if people can hear it and

04:29.939 --> 04:32.427
have time to get clear. Before you start anything,

04:32.427 --> 04:34.976
look. Check that every lock is off because the

04:34.976 --> 04:37.789
work is done, not because someone forgot.

04:37.789 --> 04:39.651
If you aren't sure everyone is clear,

04:39.651 --> 04:40.689
don't start it.

04:44.041 --> 04:46.116
Here's the short version of what would have saved

04:46.116 --> 04:48.591
this miner. Tell the people around you.

04:48.591 --> 04:51.116
Shut the equipment down at its controls.

04:51.116 --> 04:53.141
Open the disconnect for that machine,

04:53.141 --> 04:55.329
not a different one, and put your own lock and

04:55.329 --> 04:58.766
tag on it. Release or block the stored energy.

04:58.766 --> 05:01.316
Then try to start it, to prove it won't run,

05:01.316 --> 05:03.353
and put the controls back to off.

05:04.482 --> 05:07.082
Your lock stays on until you're done and clear.

05:07.082 --> 05:09.769
Only the person who put it on, or someone the company

05:09.769 --> 05:13.545
has authorized, takes it off. Module 9 walks through

05:13.545 --> 05:15.782
every step on a real conveyor.

05:16.908 --> 05:19.558
And get there the right way. Use the walkways,

05:19.558 --> 05:22.546
ladders, and platforms that are built for the job.

05:22.546 --> 05:25.683
Never walk on a conveyor belt, even a stopped one,

05:25.683 --> 05:28.445
and never climb over or under one. If there's no

05:28.445 --> 05:30.883
safe way to reach something that needs work,

05:30.883 --> 05:33.846
that's a hazard to report before the job starts,

05:33.846 --> 05:35.883
not a problem to solve by climbing.

05:37.014 --> 05:38.952
There's one exception in the standard.

05:38.952 --> 05:41.901
Some adjustments and tests, like tracking a belt,

05:41.901 --> 05:44.051
can't be done with the machine stopped.

05:44.051 --> 05:46.764
Then motion is allowed, but only to the extent

05:46.764 --> 05:50.064
the test needs it, and only if the person is effectively

05:50.064 --> 05:52.789
protected from the moving parts. That means guards

05:52.789 --> 05:55.151
stay in place, you stay outside them,

05:55.151 --> 05:57.376
and only people trained and authorized for that

05:57.376 --> 05:58.601
adjustment do it.

05:59.712 --> 06:02.987
As a new miner, you won't be doing those adjustments.

06:02.987 --> 06:05.299
If you're asked to reach into, under,

06:05.299 --> 06:07.587
or around a running machine to adjust or clean

06:07.587 --> 06:10.487
something, stop and ask. The answer should be lock

06:10.487 --> 06:11.624
it out first.

06:14.938 --> 06:17.438
You'll hear it someday. It's off, just hop up there

06:17.438 --> 06:19.988
for a second. It'll only take a minute.

06:19.988 --> 06:22.113
That's the moment this lesson is for.

06:22.113 --> 06:24.600
Off isn't locked. A minute is long enough for a

06:24.600 --> 06:27.588
timer to cycle, or for someone to hit start.

06:27.588 --> 06:29.888
Say you'll do it as soon as your lock is on.

06:29.888 --> 06:31.938
Any good lead will respect that.

06:33.064 --> 06:35.889
To sum up. A stopped machine can still start,

06:35.889 --> 06:38.939
from a timer, a remote, or another person.

06:38.939 --> 06:42.252
Before any maintenance, the machine is de-energized,

06:42.252 --> 06:44.689
locked out with your own lock, tagged,

06:44.689 --> 06:47.052
and blocked against motion, and you try to start

06:47.052 --> 06:49.927
it to prove it. You reach it by safe access,

06:49.927 --> 06:53.714
never by climbing on belts. Next, in Module 9,

06:53.714 --> 06:56.777
you'll practice the full lockout on a crusher conveyor.

06:57.910 --> 07:01.072
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

07:01.072 --> 07:02.572
override this video.
